opcua — provenance note
=======================

A record only. Nothing in this file imposes a redistribution condition beyond
zig-libs' own MIT license (see the repository `LICENSE`). Moved here from the
root `NOTICE` §2 on 2026-08-14, unchanged in substance.

Specifications (clean-room)
---------------------------

Clean-room from OPC 10000-6 (OPC UA Binary encoding + the `opc.tcp`
transport) and OPC 10000-4 (Services); both are open, royalty-free
specifications published by the OPC Foundation.

The OPC Foundation's `StatusCode.csv` / `NodeIds.csv` / `Opc.Ua.Types.bsd`
(**MIT License 1.00**) supply constants and field order.

Security is SecurityPolicy#None or Basic256Sha256 via the `rsa` module, on BOTH
the client and the server side.

Design references (behavioral/structural only, no source copied)
----------------------------------------------------------------

  - open62541 (**MPL-2.0**) — module/layering shape.
  - node-opcua (**MIT**) — client API shape.

For the server side, open62541's EXAMPLE sources (`examples/client.c`) were
read once to learn which services each demo binary exercises and which NodeIds
it addresses — behaviour and API shape only, nothing copied, and not used at
build or run time; its stock binaries were otherwise a black-box live peer.

Black-box oracles
-----------------

Additional black-box oracles used to validate the server's security: Python
`asyncua` (**LGPL-3.0**) and open62541's stock binaries — both driven as
processes whose stdout is the assertion, with no source read, built or linked —
plus `openssl` as a CLI staging a throwaway test key pair.
